To accompany the video from my recent talk at 
@aiDotEngineer
, here's an expanded version of my argument that we've seen three key inflection points with LLM over the past twelve months

Today, only 4 models set the Agent Arena Capability vs. Alignment Pareto frontier:

- GPT-6.2 Sol by 
@OpenAI

- GPT-6.2 Astra by 
@OpenAI

- GPT-6 Astra by 
@OpenAI

- Claude Fable 5.2 by 
@AnthropicAI


Every other model on the leaderboard is beaten on both by at least one of them. GPT-6.2 Sol has the highest alignment index score of 85.5; Fable 5.2 is the most capable with 1448 agent arena index score. Even flagship models such as Gemini 4 Neon or Muse Wonder Full sit below the frontier.

Do you ever wish your agent would just get on with work instead of asking questions?

We call this behavior “decision-dodging”: handing a decision back to you when the agent should have just acted on your behalf and wrapped up the task.

To understand how often it happens in practice, we selected 20 Agent Arena models across major labs.

We then counted a decision as obvious when the agent asked about something it could have decided itself, and the user simply told it to go ahead. We found that:

- Kimi K3.1 Pro by 
@Kimi_Moonshot
 and three of 
@OpenAI
’s models (GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6.2 Sol and GPT-6.2 Astra) dodge the least. They handed back an obvious decision in just 2% of sessions.

